 "content": "BOTTLENECK: the single most frequently discussed performance bottleneck across this entire reference corpus is the **`moe.all_sum` cross-rank collective** \u2014 the per-layer MoE partial-sum reduction that runs on jaccl's CPU stream and forces a GPU\u2192CPU\u2192GPU drain every layer. It is the subject of an entire dedicated section (\u00a72, \"MoE / all_sum collective \u2014 the dominant cost center\") spanning at least 20 distinct docs from 2026-05-14 through 2026-08-21, and it recurs in nearly every other section: it is the top span in the shallow-feed attribution (`moe.all_sum` 39.5% of shallow wall, with `ffn` matching it to 0.2% while `switch_mlp` is only 0.1%), it is the target of the night's biggest shipped lever (`DSV4_MOE_ALLSUM_BF16`, +3.1%",
